{"duration_api_ms":7473,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"941f55c0-615e-4790-984f-bebeb2badca3","total_cost_usd":0.022812,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":693,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1118,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1118},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":693,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1118,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.022812,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Ticket Classification & Routing: Customer Support**\n\n**Input**\n- **User ID:** user_a\n- **Query:** \"Customer requests a refund after being charged twice.\"\n\n---\n\n### 1. Classification\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **category** | `refund` (Refund / Return) |\n\n**Why:** The query contains the category keywords **\"refund\"** and **\"charged\"**, and it describes a payment problem (a duplicate charge). These match the `refund` category's keyword list. That category is also the configured `default_category`.\n\n### 2. Routing Decision\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **owner_team** | Billing Support |\n\n### 3. Priority & SLA\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **priority** | P2 |\n| **sla** | 1 business day |\n\n### 4. Policy Application\nFrozen policy: *\"Check order eligibility and payment status. If eligible, route to billing support for refund processing.\"*\n\n- **Order eligibility:** **Not determinable.** No order ID, order details, or eligibility criteria were provided.\n- **Payment status:** **Not determinable.** No transaction records were provided to confirm the duplicate charge.\n- **Result:** The ticket is assigned to Billing Support as the category owner. Refund processing depends on eligibility and payment status being verified first. No refund approval is assumed.\n\n### 5. Next Actions\n1. Check refund eligibility.\n2. Verify payment transaction status.\n3. Route to billing support if refund criteria are met.\n\n---\n\n### Missing Information (not invented)\n- Order ID or order details for the affected purchase\n- Transaction IDs, amounts, and dates of the two charges, needed to confirm a true duplicate rather than, for example, a pending authorization plus a settled charge\n- Payment method used\n- The specific refund eligibility criteria (the policy says to check eligibility but does not define the criteria)\n- Customer account or payment history for user_a\n\nIt is recommended to ask the customer for the order ID and the charge details (dates and amounts) so that verification can proceed within the 1-business-day SLA.","ttft_ms":7487,"type":"result","duration_ms":7511,"uuid":"8bb05668-c323-4c0a-b6a1-61984ac3972b","ttft_stream_ms":1602,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":1603,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
